# Core Distro staging parity follow-up

Date: 2026-10-10
Scope: private staging homepage versus the current public Core Distro site; no production changes.

## Completed corrections

- The staging homepage now omits Astra's global frontend stylesheet, which had overridden source utilities and caused dark headings, blue/oversized buttons, oversized logos, and layout collisions.
- Astra's scroll-to-top markup is removed only on the custom homepage. The normal Astra markup remains on a non-homepage route.
- The homepage header/footer logos, core colors, and click-to-scroll behavior were measured at desktop and mobile widths. No forms were submitted and the chatbot was not activated.

## Unresolved captain decisions

1. **Header at 100% zoom.** The 1440px and 1280px screenshots show the `HOME` label visually tight against/over the overflowing `PHARMACEUTICAL DISTRIBUTION` wordmark on both staging and public. The latest pass measured only anchor rectangles and claimed a 40px gap, but the wordmark has `overflow-x: visible`; that measurement does not bound the rendered tagline. A staging-only spacing correction would intentionally diverge from the current public page; modifying the live page is outside the approved staging scope. Evidence: `campaign/reports/astra-css-fix-20261010/pass3-screenshots/staging-1280x800-header.png`, `public-1280x800-header.png`, `staging-1440x900-header.png`, and `public-1440x900-header.png`.

2. **Navigation destinations.** Staging's copied homepage converts public routes into local hashes: for example, Blog goes to `#resources`, FAQ to `#contact`, and header routes to section anchors. These anchors scroll on staging, but the current public homepage routes to `/products/`, `/about/`, `/compliance/`, `/contact/`, `/resources/`, `/blog/`, and `/faq/`. The requested behavior needs a choice between linking out from the private preview to those public pages or expanding the private staging build to provide local pages. The contact/quote section is intentionally non-submitting. Evidence: `campaign/reports/astra-css-fix-20261010/pass3-screenshots/_header-debug.json`, `_nav-links.json`, `_blog-faq.json`, and `_hash-nav.json`.

## Remaining technical difference

Pass 3 reports a staging footer height of 553px versus 545px public, with identical footer top positions and an 8px total page-height delta after the Astra scroll-to-top element was removed. This is a staging difference, not established as a public-site characteristic. Its source still needs investigation before claiming exact page-height parity.

## Safety

The public site was accessed read-only. The Tailnet staging stack remained running. No production pages, forms, chatbot, credentials, DNS, firewall, proxy, cPanel, or Docker volumes were modified.
